    RTOS-MODES-3-5-DEFAULT-PRECISION-FROM-LUPREC.
  - COUPLING-CMDECHO-GATES-COMMAND-ECHO — captures the prompt output:
    CMDECHO=1 echoes the command line, CMDECHO=0 silences it while still
    running/logging the command.
  - COUPLING-MAXSORT-CAPS-ACAD-STRLSORT.
  - COUPLING-TILEMODE-CVPORT-VIEWPORT-ACCESS (vports sentinel + setview).
  - COUPLING-SNAPANG-ANGBASE-SETVAR-RADIANS.
  - COUPLING-DWGNAME-DWGPREFIX-ARE-PATH-STRINGS.
  - COUPLING-DATE-FAMILY-ARE-READABLE-REALS (DATE/TDCREATE/TDUPDATE).
  - COUPLING-SRCHPATH-ROUND-TRIPS.
  - COUPLING-TRUSTEDPATHS-SECURELOAD-ROUND-TRIP (gating itself is already
    covered by the SECURELOAD-GATE-* / SECURELOAD-FINDTRUSTEDFILE-* /
    OPEN-RESOLUTION-USES-SUPPORT-SEARCH-PATH tests).

autolisp-test conformance corpus (tests/sysvar/, profile strict), added
+ registered in harness/test-loader.lsp:

  - coupling-units.lsp: rtos modes 3-5 + UNITMODE 0/1 (+ reset).
  - coupling-sort.lsp: MAXSORT -> acad_strlsort.
  - coupling-viewport.lsp: TILEMODE/CVPORT round-trip, vports, setview.
  - coupling-command.lsp: CMDECHO round-trip; command runs under 0/1.
  - coupling-path.lsp: DWGNAME/DWGPREFIX shape, SRCHPATH round-trip.
  - coupling-angle.lsp: SNAPANG radians round-trip (added).
  - coupling-date.lsp: TDCREATE/TDUPDATE readable reals (added).

### Code change enabling the CMDECHO coupling

The mock command engine (cador/source/command-api.lisp, host-command)
previously echoed the command line unconditionally, ignoring CMDECHO —
so the "CMDECHO -> command echo" coupling was not actually wired. Added
%cador-cmdecho-on-p and gated the prompt echo on it (the command log is
still recorded unconditionally). This is the code half of that coupling;
the FiveAM + conformance tests above are the test half.

### Still open / TODO

  - rtos modes 3-5 DIMZIN feet-inch suppression bits and engineering
